# 33. IMPORTANT DEVELOPMENT RULES

These rules are mandatory.

1. Do not build only the frontend.
2. Do not create buttons that do nothing.
3. Do not use fake statistics.
4. Do not hardcode academic structures into components.
5. Do not allow students to modify administrator-defined academic categories.
6. Do not allow non-owners to edit another user's resources.
7. Require review for changes to approved academic resources.
8. Enforce PDF-only uploads on the server.
9. Make every relevant content type searchable.
10. Ensure search respects permissions and privacy.
11. Calculate trending sections from actual platform activity.
12. Do not expose private user information.
13. Do not expose administrator credentials.
14. Do not claim E2EE while chat is under development.
15. Do not require paid services for the first demonstration.
16. Do not use unnecessary AI APIs.
17. Do not generate a generic AI dashboard.
18. Keep the design consistent and professionally polished.
19. Build reusable components and maintainable code.
20. Provide clear setup instructions and environment variable examples.
21. Include database migrations and seed scripts.
22. Ensure the application can be deployed from GitHub to Vercel.
23. Do not silently replace working features with placeholders.
24. Complete and test each phase before moving to the next.

